# How tools/build-test-app.sh builds this app: as a base and split APKs, as bundletool would for Google Play, and bundled
# into build/guest/java/splits.apks (bundletool's layout) and splits.xapk (APKPure's, with an expansion file).
#
# config <qualifier>     a config split of the resources for that qualifier (aapt2 link --split): pictures for a density,
#                        strings for a language. The base keeps none of them.
# abi <abi> [real]       a split for a processor, with the app's native libraries (jni/) under lib/<abi>/; only `real`
#                        is the one they were built for, the others carry the same files under their own ABI's name
#                        (they are never run: the unpacking leaves them out)
# feature <name>         a feature split with code: split/<name>/src compiled against the base's classes
# assets <name>          an asset pack: split/<name>/assets
# obb <file>             an expansion file of the .xapk, obb/<file>, which goes to Android/obb/<package>/
config xxhdpi
config mdpi
config ldpi
config en
config ru
config de
abi armeabi_v7a real
abi arm64_v8a
abi x86
feature extra
assets pack
obb main.7.megler.test.splits.obb
